==English==
{{was wotd|2012|July|6}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|Higgs||a surname}} + {{m|en|boson}}; {{named-after|en|nat=British|occ=physicist|Peter Higgs|wplink==|nocap=1}}, who is credited with proposing what is now called the {{m|en|Higgs mechanism}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|particle}} An [[elementary particle]] in the [[Standard Model]], namely a [[boson]] with [[zero]] [[spin]], that gives [[mass]] to other [[particle]]s.
#: {{syn|en|God particle|q=informal|Higgs particle}}
#* '''1987''', Robert N. Cahn, ''The Search for a Heavy '''Higgs Boson''' at the SSC'', Orrin Fackler, J. Thanh Vân Trân (editors), ''New and Exotic Phenomena: Proceedings of the Seventh Moriond Workshop'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=duqjD3EdePEC&pg=PA468&dq=%22Higgs+boson%22|%22Higgs+bosons%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=LGf1T4WGA4XZigfQhbziBg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22Higgs%20boson%22|%22Higgs%20bosons%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 468],
#*: The existence of a '''Higgs boson''' would be the simplest solution to the problem of electroweak symmetry breaking.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Don Lincoln|title=Understanding the Universe: From Quarks to the Cosmos|page=239|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=1gFioQea39UC&pg=PA239&dq=%22Higgs+boson%22%7C%22Higgs+bosons%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=LGf1T4WGA4XZigfQhbziBg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22Higgs%20boson%22%7C%22Higgs%20bosons%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|passage=We also know other things about the '''Higgs boson'''. If it were much more massive, a problem would occur. Since '''Higgs bosons''' interact with particles with a large mass, '''Higgs bosons''' would also interact with themselves (as they have mass too). This “self interaction” puts an upper limit on the mass of the '''Higgs boson''' as less than about 500-1000 GeV.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Christopher G. Tully|title=Elementary Particle Physics in a Nutshell|page=255|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=ZBA2UgZ-MtIC&pg=PA255&dq=%22Higgs+boson%22%7C%22Higgs+bosons%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=LGf1T4WGA4XZigfQhbziBg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22Higgs%20boson%22%7C%22Higgs%20bosons%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|passage=In the higher '''Higgs boson''' mass domain, the '''Higgs boson''' decays dominantly to a pair of ''b''-quarks.}}
